sequenceDiagram
  accTitle: Delegation transfers ownership before a separate publication decision
  accDescr: On one instance, Org A requests delegation of an eligible restricted draft to Org B. The recipient reviews the request and event. Discarding leaves ownership unchanged. Accepting transfers ownership while preserving the event UUID. Acceptance does not publish the event or automatically apply the requested distribution. Org B checks the resulting content and audience before explicitly publishing. Org A may lose access after the transfer.
  actor A as Source (Org A)
  participant M as MISP
  actor B as Recipient (Org B)
  A->>M: Request delegation of eligible draft
  Note over A,M: Target organization is local
  B->>M: Review request and event content
  alt Discard the request
    B->>M: Discard delegation
    M-->>B: Ownership remains with Org A
  else Accept the handover
    B->>M: Accept delegation
    M-->>B: Ownership transferred and UUID retained
    Note over M,B: Acceptance does not publish
    B->>M: Check saved audience and content
    B->>M: Set approved audience and publish when ready
  end
  Note over A,B: Org A may lose access after transfer
